/**
@page guides Guides

@brief Architecture deep-dives - how each part actually works, beyond the
       per-class API reference.

Each guide walks a slice of the system's design and data flow with ASCII
diagrams. Start with the overviews for orientation, then dive into a specific
mechanism. The @ref main_subsystems "Subsystems" table links to each guide too.

@section guides_overview Overviews

- @subpage md_docs_2PAGES - **Pages.** The page hierarchy and the screen contract
  every full-screen view shares.
- @subpage md_docs_2EVENT__DISPATCH - **Terminal.** How input events flow from the
  serial port through the parser to the active page.
- @subpage md_docs_2LOG__FLOW - **Logging.** How a log entry travels from a call
  site through rate limiting out to every sink.

@section guides_deep Deep dives

- @subpage md_docs_2SCHEDULER__PERF - **Scheduler / Utils.** The non-blocking
  fixed-period loop, overrun handling, and the self-instrumented CPU / jitter /
  stack metrics.
- @subpage md_docs_2PLC__SYNC - **PLC I/O.** The shared-memory RX/TX state machines
  and the transactional handshake with the PLC coprocessor.
- @subpage md_docs_2EDITOR__RECONCILE - **Terminal.** How the line editor repaints
  a multi-row edit with the fewest bytes over the serial link.
*/
